WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.381
One model does the work of many.

00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:06.842
Trained once,

00:00:06.922 --> 00:00:10.302
the flow reconstructs the frequentist solution path
with a mean squared error of just zero point zero five two.

00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:13.763
When samples are scarce,

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:17.224
the sub-l-one pseudo-norms clearly beat the
Bayesian Graphical Lasso,

00:00:17.304 --> 00:00:20.685
and the gain grows as q approaches zero.

00:00:20.765 --> 00:00:24.146
Against frequentist competitors it wins at every
sample size,

00:00:24.226 --> 00:00:27.606
most at fifteen samples.

00:00:27.686 --> 00:00:31.067
Its model selection picks a lambda of three point
five two,

00:00:31.147 --> 00:00:34.528
matching the cross-validated Graphical Lasso value
of three point three six.
